WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.192 --> 00:00:01.792
(Dixieland jazz music)
- [Host] Ah, Amsterdam:

00:00:01.792 --> 00:00:04.391
the canals, the weed, the bikes.

00:00:04.391 --> 00:00:06.666
There are a lot of bikes here.

00:00:06.666 --> 00:00:10.583
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:12.264 --> 00:00:13.673
Yeah, they're everywhere.

00:00:13.673 --> 00:00:16.931
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:16.931 --> 00:00:20.023
Wait, what?
(splashing)

00:00:20.023 --> 00:00:24.155
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:24.155 --> 00:00:28.325
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:28.325 --> 00:00:30.848
There are 165 canals in Amsterdam,

00:00:30.848 --> 00:00:33.429
totaling over 60 miles in length.

00:00:33.429 --> 00:00:35.678
And resting on the ground in these canals

00:00:35.678 --> 00:00:37.761
are bikes, lots of bikes.

00:00:38.934 --> 00:00:42.851
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:47.849 --> 00:00:50.586
These two guys, they're bike fisherman.

00:00:50.586 --> 00:00:53.337
They pull bikes out of
canals in Amsterdam.

00:00:53.337 --> 00:00:57.254
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:01.596 --> 00:01:04.296
(rattling)

00:01:04.296 --> 00:01:06.262
I'm just gonna ask the obvious:

00:01:06.262 --> 00:01:07.095
Why?

00:01:07.095 --> 00:01:09.110
Why are there so many bikes in the water?

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:13.027
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:19.713 --> 00:01:23.817
The machine they use is basically
an oversized claw machine.

00:01:23.817 --> 00:01:27.209
It goes into the water
and pulls out bikes.

00:01:27.209 --> 00:01:29.933
Most bikes are found near
the edges of the canals.

00:01:29.933 --> 00:01:33.850
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:36.261 --> 00:01:38.010
And what happens after they're removed?

00:01:38.010 --> 00:01:41.927
(speaking in foreign language)

00:02:06.887 --> 00:02:09.304
(sonic beep)

